  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "A right-angled triangle has a perimeter of $56$. Find its side lengths if each of these is an integer.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$7,\\ 24,\\ 25$.\n\nTheir sum is $56$, and $7^2+24^2=25^2$.",
      "worked": "Let the shorter sides be positive integers $a\\le b$ and the hypotenuse be $c$. Then $c=56-a-b$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2+b^2&=(56-a-b)^2\\\\0&=3136-112a-112b+2ab\\\\ab-56a-56b&=-1568\\\\(56-a)(56-b)&=1568.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a+b>c$ and $c>b\\ge a$, we have $19\\le c\\le27$ and $1\\le a\\le18$. Thus $38\\le56-a\\le55$. The only divisor of $1568=2^5\\times7^2$ in this interval is $49$.\n$$\\begin{align*}56-a&=49\\\\a&=7\\\\56-b&=1568\\div49\\\\56-b&=32\\\\b&=24\\\\c&=56-7-24\\\\c&=25.\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $7+24+25=56$ and $7^2+24^2=49+576=625=25^2$. The side lengths are $7$, $24$ and $25$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 132
  },
